# ---- Outputs: NEVER commit ----
# This repo ships to sites, and every site generates its own outputs. Nothing
# under output/ is tracked: PHI artifacts never leave the site, and the PHI-free
# set reaches the coordinating centre by upload, not by git. A bare `output/` is
# deliberate -- git does not descend into an excluded directory, which is exactly
# what we want here.
output/
logs/
*.parquet
!config/*.csv

# Other sites' bundles, read by code/check_provenance.py and
# code/pool_sites.R. Bare, for the same reason output/ is bare.
#
# This matters more than output/ does, not less. These are ANOTHER
# INSTITUTION'S results, received under a DUA. They are PHI-free by
# construction, but they are not ours to publish, and this repo is public --
# so a `git add -A` after a site sends its bundle would put Rush's or
# Northwestern's output in a public repository without them having agreed
# to that.
# Added 2026-10-26: the path had been referenced in five places since
# 2026-10-02 and matched no ignore rule at all. Named multisite/ rather
# than uploads/ (SG) -- the name should say what is in it, not how it got
# there.
multisite/

# ---- R ----
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
renv/library/
renv/staging/
renv/local/
renv/cellar/

# ---- Python ----
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---- OS ----
.DS_Store

# ---- one-off validation probes: local, never committed ----
# Scratch experiments that answer a question once and are not part of the
# pipeline. Anything a run depends on belongs in code/, and anything that must
# keep being true belongs in tests/ -- which IS tracked, because both runners'
# preflight invokes it.
validation/

# ---- reference material: local reading copies, never committed ----
# Publisher PDFs and working notes. A bare `references/` like `output/` above:
# git does not descend into an excluded directory. Nothing in the repo may depend
# on a file here -- where a pointer stood in for a citation, the citation itself
# was inlined at the point of use instead.
references/

# ---- project documentation: local, never committed (SG, 2026-10-04) ----
# Principles, literature, design notes and the cohort/output specification.
# These carry unpublished measured results, and the repo is public. The repo
# ships a RUNNABLE ARTIFACT: code, config, tests and the README. Same rule as
# `references/` above -- nothing tracked may depend on a file here, so a pointer
# into docs/ from code, config or the README is a defect, not a cross-reference.
docs/

# ---- site config (contains local paths) ----
config/config.json

# ---- local session state (progress log, todo, lessons) ----
.claude/

# ---- per-site paste snippets for config.json (accepted_unhandled_dose_units) ----
config/accepted_units_*.json
